1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,139
Let us build a Digital Brain using the CarePath documents

2
00:00:04,139 --> 00:00:08,078
in our project. Start with just one file: user stories.

3
00:00:08,078 --> 00:00:12,016
We will follow one example, tracking a referral. A referral

4
00:00:12,016 --> 00:00:15,955
is a request for a patient to see another care

5
00:00:15,955 --> 00:00:19,500
team. Watch how this one file becomes connected knowledge.

6
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:24,596
After upload checks, MarkItDown converts the Word file into readable

7
00:00:24,596 --> 00:00:28,992
text. Here is the actual heading: U S zero eight,

8
00:00:28,992 --> 00:00:33,389
Track a referral, F R zero eight. Below it is

9
00:00:33,389 --> 00:00:37,785
the referral lifecycle. Django keeps this text with its source

10
00:00:37,785 --> 00:00:42,181
identifier and content fingerprint. Every extracted fact can point back

11
00:00:42,181 --> 00:00:43,500
to this file.

12
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:48,157
The normal graph begins with a document node. A node

13
00:00:48,157 --> 00:00:52,113
is simply an item. Our Python builder adds section nodes

14
00:00:52,113 --> 00:00:56,070
for the heading and ordinary text lines. Arrows connect the

15
00:00:56,070 --> 00:01:00,026
document to those sections and mean contains section. The same

16
00:01:00,026 --> 00:01:03,983
approach handles other content, including table rows and values. We

17
00:01:03,983 --> 00:01:07,939
are showing a small part of this larger graph. So

18
00:01:07,939 --> 00:01:11,500
far, we have captured the structure of the document.

19
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:16,261
Now enable optional A I enrichment. OpenAI or Claude reads

20
00:01:16,261 --> 00:01:20,322
the text and proposes typed relationships. Look at the highlighted

21
00:01:20,322 --> 00:01:24,383
heading. U S zero eight is a user story, and

22
00:01:24,383 --> 00:01:28,444
F R zero eight is a requirement. They become two

23
00:01:28,444 --> 00:01:32,505
business nodes, joined by references. The proposal carries the original

24
00:01:32,505 --> 00:01:36,566
source and exact quotation. The document structure stays in the

25
00:01:36,566 --> 00:01:40,627
graph underneath this new business layer. These links are still

26
00:01:40,627 --> 00:01:44,688
proposals at this point; evidence checks decide whether they can

27
00:01:44,688 --> 00:01:45,500
be accepted.

28
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:50,148
Now upload the architecture document. Its component table connects F

29
00:01:50,148 --> 00:01:54,097
R zero eight to domain slash referral underscore state dot

30
00:01:54,097 --> 00:01:58,045
py. That is the code module for the referral lifecycle.

31
00:01:58,045 --> 00:02:01,994
The graph grows a code node and an implemented in

32
00:02:01,994 --> 00:02:05,942
connection. Notice that F R zero eight is the same

33
00:02:05,942 --> 00:02:09,891
requirement. Next, add the traceability spreadsheet. Its row connects Test

34
00:02:09,891 --> 00:02:13,839
Lifecycle Map with F R zero eight. A test node

35
00:02:13,839 --> 00:02:17,788
grows into the graph, joined by verifies. Three different files

36
00:02:17,788 --> 00:02:21,736
now describe one connected story: what we need, where it

37
00:02:21,736 --> 00:02:24,500
is implemented, and how it is tested.

38
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:29,974
Before accepting links, the application checks the source, exact quote,

39
00:02:29,974 --> 00:02:34,747
named items, and allowed types and relationships. Matching names and

40
00:02:34,747 --> 00:02:39,521
types become one shared requirement node. Each accepted connection keeps

41
00:02:39,521 --> 00:02:44,294
its supporting document. F R zero eight joins the story,

42
00:02:44,294 --> 00:02:49,068
code, and tests. These checks filter unsupported proposals; a person

43
00:02:49,068 --> 00:02:50,500
still reviews meaning.

44
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:55,415
Prepare search adds a search structure beside the graph. With

45
00:02:55,415 --> 00:02:59,630
embeddings enabled, OpenAI converts text into a numerical vector. Watch

46
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:03,846
the text become numbers and enter the search index. The

47
00:03:03,846 --> 00:03:08,061
numbers represent meaning, not new graph facts. Later, a question

48
00:03:08,061 --> 00:03:12,276
such as, how do we test referral tracking, gets its

49
00:03:12,276 --> 00:03:16,491
own vector. Similarity search can find relevant text. Graph traversal

50
00:03:16,491 --> 00:03:20,706
follows links to the requirement and tests. These vector values

51
00:03:20,706 --> 00:03:24,500
are illustrative; unchanged text can reuse its stored vector.

52
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:29,319
Django saves a numbered draft. Graphify uses NetworkX and Leiden

53
00:03:29,319 --> 00:03:33,438
clustering to organise existing graph nodes into themes for review.

54
00:03:33,438 --> 00:03:37,557
The graph is now easier to explore across documents. Grouping

55
00:03:37,557 --> 00:03:41,676
adds organisation; it does not add new facts or prove

56
00:03:41,676 --> 00:03:42,500
a relationship.

57
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:47,994
A reviewer checks the evidence and publishes. Restricted sources are

58
00:03:47,994 --> 00:03:52,788
excluded, and retrieval checks access and current evidence again. One

59
00:03:52,788 --> 00:03:57,582
CarePath file has grown into connected stories, requirements, code, and

60
00:03:57,582 --> 00:03:59,500
tests, with supporting sources.
